    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`. The existing test suite passes, but it only checks that the labels are lower-case, so the new function isn't covered by any test. I tried to check it with a mocked client, but that command wasn't approved, so it hasn't been run against a mock or the real API.\n\nWhat it does:\n- Sends one `client.messages.create` request with `model=MODEL`, `max_tokens=5`, and the ticket text as the user message.\n- The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `LABELS`.\n- Joins the text parts of the reply, strips and lower-cases it, and returns it if it's in `LABELS`. Otherwise it returns `\"question\"`.\n\n**Temperature is set differently than you might expect.** The pinned `anthropic==1.8.0` no longer accepts `temperature` as a keyword argument to `messages.create()`. The project notes say to pass it through `extra_body`, so the code sends `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`. That field still goes into every request body, but I haven't confirmed that the API honours it this way for `claude-sonnet-4-6`. A single real call would settle that before you rely on the labeler being deterministic."
  },
